# ─── secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository is public and publishes signed packages. Same list as the
# kernel repo, for the same reason: a .gitignore is only useful for the mistake
# you have not made yet.
*.asc
*.gpg
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
handheld-repo-*
*passphrase*
*secret*
*credentials*
rclone.conf
.rclone.conf
.aws/

# The blanket *.env is for stray credential dumps, so the two kinds of .env this
# project actually uses have to be named back in. Copied from the kernel repo,
# where the only exception was sources.env; here it silently swallowed repo.env
# and every packages/*/upstream.env -- i.e. the entire upstream-tracking
# configuration -- and the loss is invisible until something reads a default.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!repo.env
!packages/*/upstream.env
*.local.*

# ─── build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/build-in-container.sh sets BUILDDIR and SRCDEST so makepkg never writes
# inside packages/, which is why there are no packages/*/src/ or packages/*/pkg/
# rules here. Those rules would also be actively wrong: decky-plugin-handheld-
# control is first-party and its src/ is TypeScript that has to be committed.
out/
.build/
.cache/
.ccache/
*.pkg.tar.zst
*.pkg.tar.zst.sig
*.pkg.tar.xz
*.pkg.tar.xz.sig

# ─── in-place JS build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# decky-plugin-handheld-control is first-party, so its PKGBUILD has an empty
# source=() and builds from $startdir directly -- BUILDDIR and SRCDEST cannot
# keep pnpm out of the package directory the way they do for downloaded sources.
#
# pnpm-lock.yaml is ignored rather than committed, which is a decision worth
# knowing about: see the note in that package's directory.
packages/*/node_modules/
packages/*/dist/
packages/*/pnpm-lock.yaml
packages/*/package-lock.json
packages/*/.pnpm/

# ─── fetched, not vendored ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# External patch sets, pulled by scripts/fetch-patch-set.sh at the ref
# pinned in each package's upstream.env. Committing them would make this a quiet
# fork of armada's work; the pinned commit is the reviewable part.
packages/*/patch-set/

# ─── generated ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.build-report.md
.upstream-report.md

packages/gtk2/

# ─── editor / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
